  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This battery is not a tank full of electricity. It stores chemical energy by moving lithium ions between two materials. During discharge, lithium ions leave the negative electrode. They travel through the electrolyte toward the positive electrode. At the same time, electrons flow through the outside circuit powering the phone. The separator lets ions pass but keeps the electrodes from touching. The electrons must take the external path. Plug in the charger and the energy pushes ions and electrons back. The battery is ready to discharge again. A battery is a control shuttle. Ions inside, electrons outside.",
